Upstream sedsubst begins with "#/bin/sh" — a malformed shebang (missing
the bang). Native builds survive because the shell's ENOEXEC fallback
runs it as a script anyway; under a qemu-user chroot that fallback does
not fire and make reports exit 127 on the colm-wrap target
(rpi400kde native pass, 2026-08-17).
--- a/sedsubst
+++ b/sedsubst
@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
-#/bin/sh
+#!/bin/sh
 #
